invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: rsa_mont.c's use_ifma answers 1 whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu
  says, so every session of an x86-64 host object runs the AVX-512 IFMA
  kernel for a modulus it takes, and dies of SIGILL on a CPU without the
  instructions. Every byte stays right, because the kernel writes
  rsa_vp1's bytes. bin/rsa_ifma_model_test counts the calls rsa_vp1_cpu
  makes into rsa_ifma_public over the lane model and requires none under
  CH_CPU_PROBED alone.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA) != 0;
--- new
    return (cpu | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA) != 0;
